  "instructions": "This project is for the TutorTrace paper (UIST 2026; PRIME Lab, Virginia Tech; advisor Yan Chen). Co-labelers: Minsun and Xiaohang. Use the uploaded submission, labeling guide, reviews and rebuttal as ground truth. Never invent numbers: if a number is not in the files or in my message, ask. Keep paper prose concise and non-hedgy; UIST style (ACM sigconf). Key facts: 87 students in a CS2 course (CS 3114), 2,340 thirty-second windows, five states incl. stalled-after-error, Light's kappa 0.71 (3 raters, computed before adjudication), TA study n=6. Talk: 2026-10-07, 15 min + 5 Q&A, session \"Learning & Tutoring\", chair Tomás Reyes.",
